A||||9||GT Bastard||Sandblasting the intake plenum.||||5||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||08-27-2000||08:14 PM||||Has anybody sandblasted thier intake plenum?  I'm wondering if the sand would put pits in that aluminum....  I was planning on having a friend sandblast it, and them polish it up nice and pretty.  I'm not a fan of chrome.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||08-27-2000||09:00 PM||||I had all of my aluminum bits bead blasted. Came out very nice. I don't know how differently sand would behave though. I would suggest getting the stuff powdercoated though, much easier to clean. The place that did mine has a polished aluminum color of powdercoat- looks just like polished aluminum without all of the labor and the benefit of that easy cleanup. Just a thought. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||08-27-2000||09:15 PM||||i had that bead blasted (glass bead media) they coated with the stuff it is now.. both the upper and middle intake pieces..(notice both are red not just the top piece) neither will effect it too much... you'll easily be able to polish it up... ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodrv6||08-27-2000||10:05 PM||||Don't use sand! It will tend to embed itself in the softer aluminum.  Glass beads or crushed walnut shells will give a very nice surface finish.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE||||reg||4
Z||000004||Cooter||08-27-2000||11:25 PM||||I learned the hard way that sandblasting would not remove the factory paint from the upper intake. Eventually I bought a large "tupper-ware" looking storage box and a gallon of paint stripper. Poured the stripper in with the intake and let it soak for about a day. Then blasted most of the paint off with a pressure washer. That factory paint/powdercoat is VERY thick! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||gtsonly||08-28-2000||08:09 AM||||i just finished sand blasting an air intake plenum! paint came off just fine, no pitting or anything. the sandblaster i use is an industrial unit and not a garage style thing. painted and all and it looks great||||reg||6
Z||000006||fierocrazy||08-29-2000||12:48 AM||||i wouldnt sand blast.  I stripped mine and glass bead it, could polish it but to lazy||||reg||1
Z||000007||gtsonly||08-29-2000||01:24 AM||||just a tad bit more info on my sandblasting of the fiero plenum. it was sandblasted with glass media or glass bends!! sorry if anyone misunderstand me||||reg||14
Z||000008||Gokart||08-29-2000||06:45 AM||||Aircraft stripper works for me. Just poured some into a thick lawn/leaf bag and dropped the plenum in. Waited a couple of hours then rinsed. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||3
Z||000009||fierocrazy||08-30-2000||04:54 PM||||we  glass bead them at the shop I work at, just becarful for smal oil passages, but the fiero intake has none, So I say blast away.  I was just remarking that the fiero red paint seem haRDER TO GET OFF THan most, just take it easy on the gasket surfaces.  the beads do remove a little metal but not to big of deal on the intaKE  MY.02||||reg||1
